{{- /* The hass-cli wrapper puts credentials in that one process's environment
       instead of exporting them from mise's [env] to everything mise spawns.
       Personal because hass-cli is only deployed there; Linux and macOS have
       neither a resolver nor a wrapper yet. See docs/home-assistant.md.

       On Windows each shell finds a different one of these under the name
       `hass-cli`. `hass-cli.cmd` is the wrapper, and what cmd finds.
       PowerShell looks for a .ps1 first, so `hass-cli.ps1` gets there ahead of
       it and fixes the quoting cmd would break. Git Bash honours no PATHEXT at
       all and would walk past both to mise's shim, so the extensionless
       `hass-cli` hands off to the .cmd. Termux needs only that last one. */}}
{{- if or (and (ne .chezmoi.os "android") (ne .chezmoi.os "windows")) (ne .hosttype "personal") }}
hass-cli
{{- end }}
{{- if or (ne .chezmoi.os "windows") (ne .hosttype "personal") }}
hass-cli.cmd
hass-cli.ps1
{{- end }}
